-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/380f415f-02ce-58d3-9c1a-f33453b9491c
-- title:
--   Full-level test function: Igusa unit, vanishing over s, annulus-unit
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q\in A.\mathrm{nonunits}$. Two function fields occur: the *floor* $\mathcal F_0:=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and the *full-level field* $\mathcal F:=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`; the hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathcal F_0\le\mathcal F$ as intermediate fields, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` is the resulting embedding. Throughout, $\hat\jmath$ denotes the element of $\mathcal F_0$ given by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the classical $j$-invariant, and a function $f$ is called *$\hat\jmath$-regular* when $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ for every place $P$ of the ambient field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,\hat\jmath$.
--
--   Further data: a finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (rational, affine geometric places whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`); a constant reduction $R_0$ of the floor, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal F_0$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, extending the residue map of $A$ on constants, a place map preserving degrees and compatible with divisors, and the scaling property that every nonzero element of $\mathcal F_0$ can be multiplied by a constant so as to lie in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` is the Gauss-reduction compatibility: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathcal F_0$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   There are in addition: a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`; a family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}:\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\to$ valuation subrings of $\mathcal F$; a family $O^{\mathrm{SS}}:W\to$ valuation subrings of $\mathcal F$. The *Igusa group* of hypotheses: `hIg_inf` describes $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the line `lineInfty q` as the set of $f\in\mathcal F$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ coefficientwise in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$; `hIg` asserts that every line $\ell$ is $\gamma$-translate of `lineInfty q` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ under `redQ q`, with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$; `hIg_perm` asserts that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The *supersingular group*: `hSS_A` states that a constant of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ precisely when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` states that for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is $\hat\jmath$-regular and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` states that each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t\in O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   One place $s\in W$ is then fixed, together with a field $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ over the residue field of $A$ containing an element transcendental over it (`htr`), and a component chart $C_b$ of $\mathcal F$ with values in $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ whose ring of integers is $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ (`hCb`); a `ComponentChart` consists of a valuation subring, a residue map onto $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ with kernel the maximal ideal and extending the residue map of $A$, a set `dom` of places, a finset `nodes`, a place map avoiding the nodes on `dom`, the scaling property, and the pointwise and divisor compatibilities.
--
--   The *annulus group*: two families $An',An:\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\to$ `Annulus A ↥(fieldBar q M')` (each annulus being a set of places, a parameter and a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the axioms of that structure), and an injective family of places $xt(\ell)$ of $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ over the residue field of $A$ (`hxt_inj`). The hypothesis `hAn` says that for every $\ell$ the annuli $An'(\ell)$ and $An(\ell)$ have the same domain and the same modulus, that this modulus is nonzero in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and that the product of their parameters is that modulus, so the two parameters are reciprocal. The hypothesis `hxt_att` says that for each $\ell$ the parameter of $An'(\ell)$ lies in the integers of the regular prolongation underlying $C_b$ (same integers and residue map), its residue has order $1$ at $xt(\ell)$, and for every $f$ in those integers with nonzero residue and with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f=0$ at all $P$ in the domain of $An'(\ell)$, and every such $P$, the product $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\cdot P.\mathrm{evalAt}((An'\ell).\mathrm{param})^{-\mathrm{ord}_{xt(\ell)}(\text{residue of }f)}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there; these are the clauses of `IsAttached` other than membership of $xt(\ell)$ in the nodes of $C_b$. The hypothesis `hAn_tube` places the annuli in the tube of $s$: for every $\ell$, every place $P$ in the domain of $An'(\ell)$, every $\hat\jmath$-regular $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue is the value at $s$ of that residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Finally the test datum. An element $J\in\mathcal F$ is given whose Laurent expansion is `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`, the series obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by multiplying every exponent by $q$ (`hJ`), subject to `hJreg`: $J$ is $\hat\jmath$-regular as an element of $\mathcal F$, i.e. $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,J$ at every place $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\hat\jmath$. The Hasse-invariant datum `hHasse` asserts the existence of $a_0\in A$ such that $J-a_0$ lies in $C_b.\mathrm{integers}$ with $C_b$-residue $0$, and of $c'\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $c'\cdot(J-a_0)$ lies in $C_b.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero $C_b$-residue, and such that for every line $\ell$ there are a field $F_I$ over the residue field of $A$, a component chart $C$ of $\mathcal F$ with values in $F_I$ and a place $x$ of $F_I$ over that residue field with $C.\mathrm{integers}=O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$, with $An(\ell)$ attached to $C$ at $x$ in the sense of `IsAttached`, and with $J-a_0\in C.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero $C$-residue satisfying
--   $$\mathrm{ord}_{xt(\ell)}\bigl(C_b\text{-residue of }c'(J-a_0)\bigr)=-\,\mathrm{ord}_{x}\bigl(C\text{-residue of }J-a_0\bigr).$$
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every line $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ there exists $g\in\mathcal F$ such that (i) $g\neq 0$; (ii) $g$ is $\hat\jmath$-regular, i.e. $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,g$ for every place $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\hat\jmath$; (iii) $g$ lies in $C_b.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $C_b$-residue is $0$; (iv) both $g$ and $g^{-1}$ lie in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$, that is, $g$ is a unit of the Igusa ring of the line $\ell$; and (v) $P.\mathrm{ord}\,g=0$ for every place $P$ in the domain of $An'(\ell)$.
--
--   This produces, for each line of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$, a rational function on the full-level curve $X_H(q^2M')$ that reduces to zero on the supersingular component chart, is a unit on the Igusa ring of that line, and has no zeros or poles on the reciprocal tube annulus — the test function used to separate the Igusa components from the supersingular component. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted), the construction of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve at $q$; the fact that the ambient field is a curve of essentially finite type over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ comes from [`ModularCurve.isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField).
